#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161745 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "6d3ad56f-a242-5335-aa48-e2608b1b973d" :question/math-academy-id "e-16584" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(1\\right)$, calculate $P\\left(X < 2\\right)$. Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{λe^{- λx},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left(1 \\right)\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{e^{-x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate\n\n$$\nP\\left(X < 2\\right)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X < 2) &= \\int_{0}^{2}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{2}e^{-x}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.- e^{-x}\\right|_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&=-e^{-2} + e^{0} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.8647\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161746 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161931 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1677dd6-74e4-5778-bbba-fbb230c7646a" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Greater Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "f1adfc5c-78aa-5f14-bec5-cf763d86e5af" :question/math-academy-id "e-16585" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(\\dfrac 23\\right)$, calculate $P\\left(X \\geq 3\\right)$. Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{λe^{- λx},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left(\\dfrac 23 \\right)\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{\\frac{2}{3}e^{-2x/3},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate\n\n$$\nP\\left(X \\geq 3\\right)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\ge 3) &= \\int_{3}^{∞}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{3}^{∞}\\frac{2}{3}e^{-2x/3}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.- e^{-2x/3}\\right|_{3}^{∞} \\\\\n&= e^{-2} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.1353\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161747 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161932 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c89beba-5605-514e-82c3-8e8145b178c9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability on a Bounded Interval Using the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "fffe6dba-c0a1-5644-a975-6d51b6de2f98" :question/math-academy-id "e-16586" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(2\\right)$, calculate $P\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right)$. Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{λe^{- λx},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX\\sim \\textrm{Exp} \\left(2 \\right)\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{2e^{-2x},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0 \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate\n\n$$\nP\\left(\\dfrac 12 < X < 2\\right)\n$$\n\nas follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(\\frac{1}{2} < X < 2) &= \\int_{1/2}^{2}f(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{1/2}^{2}2e^{-2x}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.- e^{-2x}\\right|_{1/2}^{2} \\\\\n&=-e^{-4} + e^{-1} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.3496\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161748 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aab06631-cd2c-57d2-9518-25f7a31c4b6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Probabilities Using the Memoryless Property"}] :question/id #uuid "88232e58-999e-5ac8-8f09-8a4b204ec51c" :question/math-academy-id "e-16587" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X\\sim \\textrm{Exp}\\left(4\\right)$, calculate $P\\left(X \\leq 7 \\, \\bigg \\mid \\, X > 5\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X \\sim \\mathrm{Exp}(\\lambda)$ and two positive real numbers $s, t$, the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t \\, \\big \\mid \\, X>s) = P(X > t) = e^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\leq s+t \\, \\big \\mid \\, X>s) = 1-P(X>s+t \\, \\big \\mid \\, X>s) = 1-e^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda = 4\n$$\n\n$s=5$, and\n\n$$\ns+t=7\n$$\n\nFrom this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt = (t+s) - s =7 - 5 = 2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\le 7 \\mid X > 5) &= 1 - e^{- λt} \\\\\n&= 1 - e^{- (4) \\cdot (2)} \\\\\n&= 1 - e^{-8} \\\\\n&\\approx 0.999664\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161930 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc5827c-739e-52fd-9f10-a75bf2c18c22" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a \"Less Than\" Probability With the Exponential Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b36bf296-2266-53e1-ae35-e8fa637db296" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2650" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161403} {:answer/id #uuid "d4524de5-3262-560c-b7b4-1f0fe461930f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2889" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161404} {:answer/id #uuid "eedb40f3-78bd-5fd3-9379-cf524faf4299" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186161405} {:answer/id 